  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47268\", \"PowerToys#47534\", \"PowerToys#48038\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. Grab and Move doesn't currently work with FancyZones. When you drag a window with Grab and Move, the FancyZones overlay doesn't appear, whether you hold Shift or have Shift activation turned off. The maintainers closed the later reports as duplicates of PowerToys#47268, so that issue is the one to follow. Add a thumbs-up or a comment there instead of opening a new ticket. Until the integration exists, drag the window by its title bar to snap it to a zone. You can also use FancyZones' keyboard snapping, which is Win+Arrow if you've enabled the override for Windows Snap.\"}",
